#You probably will have to modify these. Download the file, and make sure this navigates to the correct files on your device, and corresponds to the particular OS you're using- how addresses work differ for Windows and Linux
read_verilog ./a2o-master/dev/verilog/unisims_synth
read_verilog -I./a2o-master/dev/verilog/trilib ./a2o-master/dev/verilog/trilib/*
read_verilog -I./a2o-master/dev/verilog/trilib ./a2o-master/dev/verilog/work/*
proc          
opt 

#You can remove this block if you have to- it's time intensive and really are just additional optimization steps, but I recommend at least opt_clean and opt_expr
opt_clean
opt_expr
opt_reduce     
opt_merge

#Memory handling steps, pretty standard
memory
memory_libmap  
techmap 

# Aggressive cleanup steps- again, optional, but if you want the smallest, least redundant netlist, it's probably best to have. 
clean
opt_clean    
setundef -zero 
opt          

abc -liberty      #VERY IMPORTANT: Modify this if you want a different process. Look up Yosys' inbuilt libraries, and pick the one you need. You can make actual GDSII files- as in production-ready IC designs- if you reference a library Yosys has for a process that's actually manufactureable

#Another cleanup step. Very, very redundant, but it's good to be paranoid about these things. You can probably remove these with zero effect.
clean
opt_clean

write_verilog -noattr netlist.v #Name the file whatever you want
